<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abraham Lincoln</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1809">1809</a>–<a href="/years/1865">1865</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abraham Lincoln was the 16th president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, from 1861 until his assassination in 1865. His election as a Republican opposed to the expansion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> led Southern states to secede, and he led the Union through the Civil War. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emancipation-proclamation">Emancipation Proclamation</a> of 1863 and support for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirteenth-amendment">Thirteenth Amendment</a> brought about the abolition of slavery.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln.jpg" alt="Abraham Lincoln" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Gardner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abraham_Lincoln_O-77_matte_collodion_print.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
